From 5576f6bb3fd2ca04e5d93441bc3deff2cc0461b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:13:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Set \@currentlabelname for captions (title for named
 references)

Optional, and not meant for the series itself.

\@caption stores the list text in \@currentlabelname, so that a \label
after a caption records it as the title for named references, as for
headings. \caption* does not change it, just as it keeps \@currentlabel:
a \label after a \caption* that follows a numbered caption in the same
float records the title (and number) of that caption; usrguide says not
to use \label after \caption*. Before, with \DocumentMetadata and
hyperref, the title of the last heading was recorded. This changes the
third field of \newlabel for labelled captions, also in documents
without any package.

Known problem: the title is the raw list text, not a sanitised one, in
every case (with \DocumentMetadata and hyperref, and without packages,
too): for example a \label inside the caption text ends up in the title
field, and ltxref.dtx says that \@currentlabelname should typically
contain a sanitised title. memoir (\M@gettitle) and nameref without
hyperref (\NR@gettitle) set a cleaned title before they call the kernel
\@caption, which this then overwrites. A # in the list text gives more
errors than before. So it may be better done by nameref/hyperref in the
hook caption/prepare, which runs at the same place, or in the kernel
only with a sanitised title and only if no wrapper has set one.

Documentation: the description of caption/prepare says that
\@currentlabelname is set; a paragraph in the \@caption section.

Tests: new base test caption-interface-008 (\@currentlabelname after
\caption, with an optional argument, after \caption* and without
packages). latex-lab float-023 also prints \nameref of four captions.
The expected output changes in the title field of \newlabel in
float-002, float-003, float-004, float-007-gh55, float-tagging-off,
float-023 and float-024, and in the firstaid test
firstaid-cleveref-1684.
